**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitProxyTests`

**How to implement.** The kit-folder seam in Domain: its record over the kit file, and its in-memory double over a shared in-memory folder (001 §P: `KitProxy`, built per opened folder; 001 §F 'New kit…: … An empty folder is initialised; a folder that already has files keeps them, and .kit-json plus the app's subfolders are added'; .spec-md §4: every proxy has an in-memory implementation of the same shape; §5 `KitProxy`: 'Fields grow as kinds land'). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`: `module KitFolders` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `Kit.fs` (step 122): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `Kit` and `LibraryEntryFiles`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.1. (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitProxy = { initialiseKit : KitFile -> Result<unit, KitError>; readKitFile : unit -> Result<KitFile, KitError>; writeKitFile : KitFile -> Result<unit, KitError> }`, the functional-proxy convention of `ElementId.fs:583` (`SourceProxy`): one proxy per kit folder, built once where the folder is opened. Each field has a one-line doc. `initialiseKit` makes the folder a kit: it refuses a folder that already holds a `.kit-json` with `KitAlreadyExistsErr` and writes nothing; otherwise it keeps every file and folder the folder holds and adds the folders `data` and `library` and the kit file. `readKitFile` answers the kit file, or `NotAKitFolderErr` when there is none. `writeKitFile` replaces the kit file whole, or answers `NotAKitFolderErr`, writing nothing, when the folder is not a kit yet, so `initialiseKit` is the one way a folder becomes a kit. (2) `InMemoryKitFolder`, one in-memory kit folder that every in-memory proxy built over it shares, as two windows share one folder. Its content (the kit file, texts by their kit-relative path, the folders that exist and, from step 129, the lock) is state private to it, mutated only inside its members and the proxies' closures, the boundary as in `ElementId.fs:1101` (`SourceProxy.createInMemory`). Its public surface is: `static member create () : InMemoryKitFolder`, a folder that exists and holds nothing; `member this.placeLabFile (path : KitRelativePath) (text : KitFileText) : Result<unit, KitError>`, an outside writer placing or replacing a text at a path and adding its parent folders (the `.kit-json` path is refused with `InvalidKitPathErr`, because only `initialiseKit` and `writeKitFile` write the kit file); and `member this.paths () : KitRelativePath list`, every file and folder it holds (the `.kit-json`, each text and each of its parent folders, each folder added), in ordinal order. One map of texts by path serves every text a later step stores, so a kit file of a kind (step 127) is the text at its file name and a lab file is the text at its path, as in a real folder. (3) `type KitProxy with static member createInMemory (folder : InMemoryKitFolder) : KitProxy`, the double (.spec-md §4). Its three fields follow (1) over the folder's state; the folder it names in an error's reason is `in-memory kit folder`. No caching, retry or other field is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitProxyTests.fs`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests` (test code is outside the ELEV scope). It declares, each with a one-line doc: a test-local record `KitTestFolder = { openProxy : unit -> KitProxy; placeLabFile : string -> string -> unit; paths : unit -> string list }`, one folder as the facts see it: `openProxy` builds a NEW proxy over the same folder each call, as a second window or process would; `placeLabFile path text` is an outside writer (an instrument, another editor) placing a file at a kit-relative path; `paths` lists every file and folder under the kit, kit-relative with forward slashes, in ordinal order. `steppingClock () : ClockProvider` starts at `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)` and advances one second per call. `newKitFile (clock : ClockProvider) : KitFile` is `KitFile.create` over `KitId (Guid.Parse "6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e25-9a41-0c8d5e7f2b16")`, `Optics: QZ/LR` and `KitAuthor "Test author"` at `clock.now ()`. `[<AbstractClass>] type KitProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshFolder : unit -> KitTestFolder`, a folder that exists and holds nothing, and holds the contract facts; `type KitProxyTests () = inherit KitProxyContract ()` answers a fresh `InMemoryKitFolder.create ()` whose `openProxy` is `KitProxy.createInMemory` over it, whose `placeLabFile` goes through `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` and `placeLabFile`, and whose `paths` renders `paths ()`. The facts: `a folder holds no kit until it is initialised`: `readKitFile` of a fresh folder answers `NotAKitFolderErr`, `writeKitFile` answers `NotAKitFolderErr`, and `paths` is empty. `initialising an empty folder writes the kit file, data and library, and nothing else`: after `initialiseKit (newKitFile clock)`, `paths` is exactly `.kit-json`, `data` and `library`, and `readKitFile` answers the kit file given. `initialising a folder that holds files keeps every one of them`: with `notes.txt` and `raw/run 1.csv` placed first, `initialiseKit` answers `Ok`, and `paths` is exactly `.kit-json`, `data`, `library`, `notes.txt`, `raw` and `raw/run 1.csv` (.spec-md §3.13: AT-1 builds its kit around its lab folder). `a folder that already holds a kit is not initialised again`: a second `initialiseKit`, of another kit file and through a second proxy, answers `KitAlreadyExistsErr`; `readKitFile` still answers the first and `paths` is unchanged. `the kit file is replaced in place and read back equal`: `writeKitFile` of the kit file with `notes = KitNotes "Reviewed"` and `sendExclude = [ SendExcludeGlob "**/*.dng" ]` answers `Ok`, and `readKitFile` of a second proxy answers it.

**Acceptance.** After the seam lands, `KitFolders.fs` MUST declare `KitProxy` with exactly `initialiseKit`, `readKitFile` and `writeKitFile`, `InMemoryKitFolder` and `KitProxy.createInMemory`, and `KitProxyContract` MUST hold the kit-file facts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a folder holds no kit until it is initialised`, `initialising an empty folder writes the kit file, data and library, and nothing else`, `initialising a folder that holds files keeps every one of them`, `a folder that already holds a kit is not initialised again`, `the kit file is replaced in place and read back equal` under `KitProxyTests`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.
